schema: "0.4"
id: sem-data-query-ux-design
type: image
quality: high
product_targets:
  - semtext.dev
tags:
  - semtext
  - sem-data-query
  - ux-design
  - reference

prompt:
  text: |
    UX design sheet for the SemText `<sem-data-query>` element — the editable
    default query inside a data visualizer, rendered in the minimal-tech-light
    theme on a dark slate canvas (bg #0f172a, surface #1e293b, fg #e2e8f0,
    muted #cbd5e1, border #334155, accent #60a5fa). The sheet shows FOUR stacked
    example cards, each inside a rounded 12px surface with a hairline border and
    a small mono uppercase caption above it.

    Every card opens with the same context above the query chrome: a rendered
    data table captioned "services" with columns NAME / PORT / READY and three
    rows (api 8443 true, web 8080 true, metrics 9090 false) — the visualizer's
    source bucket — and, above that table, the authored markdown as a thin
    monospace source strip. Below the table sits the query block the card is
    about: a small mono caption line reading "QUERY — SELECT … FROM <bucket>
    (WHERE / ORDER BY / LIMIT)", an editable multi-line monospace textarea
    holding the query, a compact "Run" button, a status line, and a generated
    results table.

    Card 1 — caption "DEFAULT (RESULT SET)". The textarea reads
    "SELECT name, port FROM services WHERE ready = true ORDER BY port LIMIT 5".
    The status line reads "2 rows." and the results table shows two rows:
    web 8080 and api 8443, with a small sort caret in each results column
    header. The query statement stays fully legible in the textarea.

    Card 2 — caption "EDITED (RE-RUN ON INPUT)". The same visualizer, but the
    textarea now reads "SELECT name FROM services" (the user edited it). The
    status line reads "3 rows." and the results table shows three rows
    (api, web, metrics) under a single NAME column — the query re-ran because
    the text was edited.

    Card 3 — caption "ERROR (UNKNOWN BUCKET)". The textarea reads
    "SELECT name FROM hosts" — a bucket this visualizer does not define. The
    status line reads "The query failed to run." and directly beneath it, in
    the accent-red family (#f87171 / #ef4444, not neon), a single inline error
    line reads: `sem-data-query: unknown bucket "hosts" — buckets in this
    visualizer: services`. No results table. The authored query text is still
    fully readable in the textarea.

    Card 4 — caption "JS-OFF / PLAIN TEXT". No chrome at all: the visualizer's
    markdown source and the query statement appear as ordinary document text
    (the raw `| name | port | ready |` table lines and the sentence
    "SELECT name, port FROM services WHERE ready = true ORDER BY port LIMIT 5"),
    nothing hidden, nothing generated, no buttons or textarea.

    Typography: clean system sans for captions and status, monospace for query
    text and table cells, generous margins. Chrome is minimal — one caption
    line, one textarea, one button, one status line, one table.

  negative: >
    occluded, dimmed or blurred query text; the textarea rendered as a code
    block that hides the statement; syntax-highlighting rainbow inside the
    query; neon glow or drop shadows on text; more than four cards; light
    background; watermark; lorem ipsum in the captions; invented buttons or
    toolbars beyond Run; a results table drawn on the error or JS-off card;
    a raw SQL exception/stack trace instead of the single inline error line.

  style: >
    Flat UI spec sheet, minimal-tech aesthetic, restrained single-accent
    palette, crisp 12px card radius, hairline #334155 borders, generous
    negative space. Looks like a panel from a design-system guide describing
    one component in its states.

attachments:
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-data-query/sem-data-query-enhanced-primary-960.png
    role: reference
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-data-query/sem-data-query-enhanced-error-960.png
    role: reference
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-data-query/sem-data-query-nojs-fixture-1000.png
    role: reference

output:
  dimensions:
    width: 1536
    height: 1024
    aspect_ratio: "3:2"
  formats:
    - format: png
      filename: sem-data-query-ux-design.png

requirements:
  modes:
    - id: default
      label: "DEFAULT (RESULT SET)"
      must_show:
        - an editable monospace textarea holding the full SELECT statement
        - a "Run" button and a status line reading "2 rows."
        - a results table with two rows (web 8080, api 8443) and sort carets
      must_never:
        - dim, blur or occlude the query statement
        - show an error line or an empty results table
    - id: edited
      label: "EDITED (RE-RUN ON INPUT)"
      must_show:
        - a textarea holding "SELECT name FROM services"
        - a status line reading "3 rows." and a three-row NAME-only results table
      must_never:
        - show the original WHERE/ORDER BY/LIMIT statement (it was edited)
        - leave the results stale at two rows
    - id: error
      label: "ERROR (UNKNOWN BUCKET)"
      must_show:
        - a textarea holding "SELECT name FROM hosts"
        - a status line "The query failed to run."
        - one inline accent-red error line naming the unknown bucket and the
          buckets the visualizer does define
      must_never:
        - render a results table in the error state
        - hide or dim the authored query text
        - show a stack trace or raw exception
    - id: js-off
      label: "JS-OFF / PLAIN TEXT"
      must_show:
        - the markdown table source and the query statement as ordinary text
      must_never:
        - show the textarea, Run button, status line or results table
        - hide or alter the authored text

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.75
  criteria:
    query-legibility:
      weight: 0.35
      description: >
        The query statement reads at full contrast in the textarea on every
        card; the query is the most legible thing in the block.
      fail_signals:
        - query text dimmed, blurred or occluded
        - textarea rendered as an opaque block hiding the statement
        - rainbow syntax colouring that lowers contrast
    chrome-fidelity:
      weight: 0.3
      description: >
        Each card carries exactly the chrome its state defines — caption line,
        textarea, Run button, status line, results table — with the tabular
        state matching the statement.
      fail_signals:
        - invented controls beyond Run
        - status text disagreeing with the results-table row count
        - results table shown on the error or JS-off card
    state-distinction:
      weight: 0.2
      description: >
        default (2 rows), edited (3 rows, NAME-only), error (inline message,
        no table) and JS-off (plain text) are visually distinct and match their
        captions.
      fail_signals:
        - default and edited cards identical
        - error card missing the inline error line
        - JS-off card showing interactive chrome
    spec-sheet-quality:
      weight: 0.15
      description: >
        Reads as a component design sheet: four labeled cards, consistent
        monospace, dark minimal-tech palette, no decorative noise.
      fail_signals:
        - watermark, lorem ipsum, neon glow
        - more or fewer than four labeled cards
  reject_if:
    - any card occludes, blurs or bars the query statement
    - the error card renders a results table or a stack trace
    - the JS-off card shows the textarea, Run button or results table